            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "The belt and deck surface wear first, as they are designed to. The failure that usually ends a pad is the motor or its controller, damaged by heat that builds when the deck runs dry or the pad is worked near its limits for long periods. Remotes and app connections can also retire an otherwise healthy pad.",
